Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$ be a doubly-connected domain with boundary components $\alpha$ and $\beta$, and let $z_0, z_1 \in D$. Let $A, B \in \mathbb{R}$ be given real numbers. Consider the class $\mathcal{F}$ of all functions $u \colon D \to [-\infty, \infty)$ such that:
\begin{itemize}
\item $u$ is subharmonic in $D$;
\item $u$ extends continuously to $\alpha \cup \beta$ with boundary values $u \equiv A$ on $\alpha$ and $u \equiv B$ on $\beta$;
\item there exists a curve $\gamma \subset \overline{D}$ joining $z_1$ to a point of $\alpha$ along which $u \le 0$.
\end{itemize}
Determine
\[
\sup_{u \in \mathcal{F}} u(z_0),
\]
and identify the extremal function (if one exists).

